.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-priority=\fINICE\fB\fR sets the ovn-northd process niceness\[char46] The default is \fB\-10\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs ovn-northd under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-priority=\fINICE\fB\fR sets the ovn-controller process niceness\[char46] The default is \fB\-10\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs ovn-controller under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-priority=\fINICE\fB\fR sets the ovn-ic process niceness\[char46] The default is \fB\-10\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs ovn-ic under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-priority=\fINICE\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller process niceness\[char46] The default is \fB\-10\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs ovn-br-controller under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovsdb\-nb\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs the Northbound database server under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovsdb\-sb\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs the Southbound database server under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovsdb\-ovnbr\-wrapper=\fIWRAPPER\fB\fR runs the OVN bridge controller database server under the specified wrapper\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-user=\fIUSER[:GROUP]\fB\fR runs OVN daemons as the specified user and optional group\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-manage\-ovsdb=\fIyes|no\fB\fR controls whether \fBstart_northd\fR and \fBstop_northd\fR also manage the NB and SB database servers\[char46] The default is \fByes\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-system\-id=\fISYSTEM_ID\fB\fR sets the chassis name passed to ovn-controller\[char46] The default is empty\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovsdb\-disable\-file\-column\-diff=\fIyes|no\fB\fR controls whether database servers are started with \fB\-\-disable\-file\-column\-diff\fR\[char46] The default is \fBno\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR displays usage information\[char46]
.SH "FILE LOCATION OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR sets the local Open vSwitch database socket\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Northbound database file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Southbound database file\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR and \fB\-\-db\-sb\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR set the NB and SB database sockets\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnnb_db\[char46]sock\fR and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnsb_db\[char46]sock\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-schema=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Northbound database schema file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-schema=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Southbound database schema file\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR and \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR set the IC-NB and IC-SB database sockets\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_nb_db\[char46]sock\fR and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_sb_db\[char46]sock\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
.PP
The \fB\-\-db\-nb\-create\-insecure\-remote=\fIyes|no\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-sb\-create\-insecure\-remote=\fIyes|no\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-create\-insecure\-remote=\fIyes|no\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-create\-insecure\-remote=\fIyes|no\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-create\-insecure\-remote=\fIyes|no\fB\fR options accept \fByes\fR or \fBno\fR\[char46] The default is \fBno\fR\[char46] When set to \fByes\fR, the database server creates an insecure ptcp remote; \fBno\fR does not create that remote\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-NB database file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-SB database file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-schema=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-NB database schema file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-schema=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-SB database schema file\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR and \fB\-\-db\-sb\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR set the NB and SB database pidfiles\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnnb_db\[char46]pid\fR and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnsb_db\[char46]pid\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR and \fB\-\-db\-sb\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR set the NB and SB database control sockets\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnnb_db\[char46]ctl\fR and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnsb_db\[char46]ctl\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-config\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Northbound database server configuration file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-config\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Southbound database server configuration file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-config\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-NB database server configuration file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-config\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the IC-SB database server configuration file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-config\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the Southbound relay server configuration file\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-use\-remote\-in\-db\fR, \fB\-\-db\-sb\-use\-remote\-in\-db\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-use\-remote\-in\-db\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-use\-remote\-in\-db\fR accept \fByes\fR or \fBno\fR and default to \fByes\fR\[char46] A bare option is equivalent to specifying \fByes\fR\[char46] The value \fByes\fR makes ovsdb-server listen on remotes configured in the database \fBconnections\fR column, while \fBno\fR does not\[char46] If a corresponding configuration file is specified, it takes precedence and this setting is ignored\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-use\-remote\-in\-db=\fIyes|no\fB\fR controls whether ovsdb-server listens on the remotes configured in the database \fBconnections\fR column\[char46] The default is \fByes\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-key=\fIKEY\fB\fR sets the ovn-controller SSL/TLS private key file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-controller SSL/TLS certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-ca\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-controller SSL/TLS CA certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-bootstrap\-ca\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR bootstraps the ovn-controller SSL/TLS CA certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-key=\fIKEY\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS private key file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-ca\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS CA certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-bootstrap\-ca\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR bootstraps the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS CA certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-key=\fIKEY\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database SSL/TLS private key file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database SSL/TLS certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-ca\-cert=\fICERT\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database SSL/TLS CA certificate file\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR sets the OVN bridge controller database socket\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-file=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the OVN bridge controller database file\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR set the IC-NB, IC-SB, and OVN bridge controller database pidfiles\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_nb_db\[char46]pid\fR, \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_sb_db\[char46]pid\fR, and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnbr_db\[char46]pid\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR set database control sockets\[char46] Their defaults are \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_nb_db\[char46]ctl\fR, \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovn_ic_sb_db\[char46]ctl\fR, and \fBOVN_RUNDIR/ovnbr_db\[char46]ctl\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-schema=\fIFILE\fB\fR sets the OVN bridge controller database schema file\[char46]
.SH "LOGGING OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR set daemon logging parameters\[char46] The default is \fB\-vconsole:emer \-vsyslog:err \-vfile:info\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR sets ovn-br-controller logging parameters\[char46] The default is \fB\-vconsole:emer \-vsyslog:err \-vfile:info\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-relay\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-log=\fISTRING\fB\fR set database-server logging parameters\[char46] The defaults for the NB, SB, IC-NB, IC-SB, and OVN bridge controller database servers are \fB\-vconsole:off \-vfile:info\fR\[char46] The default for the SB relay database server is \fB\-vconsole:emer \-vsyslog:err \-vfile:info\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, \fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-relay\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-logfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR select log files\[char46] Database-server log files default to files under \fBOVN_LOGDIR\fR; daemon log files default to empty\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-n\-threads=\fIN_THREADS\fB\fR sets the number of ovn-northd threads\[char46] The default is \fB1\fR\[char46]
.SH "PROTOCOL, CIPHER AND CIPHERSUITE OPTIONS"
.PP
.PP
The daemon and database prefixes also accept their SSL/TLS key, certificate, and CA certificate options\[char46] The prefixes are \fBovn\-controller\fR, \fBovn\-northd\fR, \fBovn\-ic\fR, \fBovn\-nb\-db\fR, \fBovn\-sb\-db\fR, \fBovn\-ic\-nb\-db\fR, \fBovn\-ic\-sb\-db\fR, \fBovn\-sb\-relay\-db\fR, and \fBovn\-ovnbr\-db\fR; append \fB\-ssl\-key\fR, \fB\-ssl\-cert\fR, or \fB\-ssl\-ca\-cert\fR\[char46] Controller prefixes also accept \fB\-ssl\-bootstrap\-ca\-cert\fR\[char46] Empty values leave the normal database or daemon TLS settings in effect\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-controller\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-sb\-relay\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-server\-name=\fINAME\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS protocols\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller SSL/TLS cipher list\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnbr\-controller\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller TLS 1\[char46]3 and later ciphersuite list\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-protocols=\fIPROTOCOLS\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database SSL/TLS protocols\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-ciphers=\fICIPHERS\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database SSL/TLS cipher list\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-ovnbr\-db\-ssl\-ciphersuites=\fICIPHERSUITES\fB\fR sets the ovn-br-controller database TLS 1\[char46]3 and later ciphersuite list\[char46]
.SH "ADDRESS AND PORT OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-sync\-from\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-sync\-from\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-sync\-from\-proto=\fIPROTO\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-sync\-from\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-sync\-from\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-sync\-from\-proto=\fIPROTO\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-sync\-from\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-sync\-from\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-sync\-from\-proto=\fIPROTO\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-sync\-from\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-sync\-from\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-sync\-from\-proto=\fIPROTO\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
The options \fB\-\-db\-nb\-addr\fR, \fB\-\-db\-nb\-port\fR, \fB\-\-db\-sb\-addr\fR, \fB\-\-db\-sb\-port\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-addr\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-port\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-addr\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-port\fR, \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-addr\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-port\fR select the addresses and ports used when the corresponding \fB\-\-db\-*\-create\-insecure\-remote\fR option is \fByes\fR\[char46] When that option is \fBno\fR, these settings have no effect\[char46] The defaults for \fB\-\-db\-nb\-addr\fR and \fB\-\-db\-nb\-port\fR are \fB0\[char46]0\[char46]0\[char46]0\fR and \fB6641\fR, respectively\[char46] The defaults for \fB\-\-db\-sb\-addr\fR and \fB\-\-db\-sb\-port\fR are \fB0\[char46]0\[char46]0\[char46]0\fR and \fB6642\fR, respectively\[char46] The defaults for \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-addr\fR and \fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-port\fR are \fB0\[char46]0\[char46]0\[char46]0\fR and \fB6645\fR, respectively\[char46] The defaults for \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-addr\fR and \fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-port\fR are \fB0\[char46]0\[char46]0\[char46]0\fR and \fB6646\fR, respectively\[char46] The defaults for \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-addr\fR and \fB\-\-db\-ovnbr\-port\fR are \fB0\[char46]0\[char46]0\[char46]0\fR and \fB6651\fR, respectively\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-nb\-db\fR and \fB\-\-ovn\-northd\-sb\-db\fR select the NB and SB remotes used by ovn-northd\[char46] Similarly, \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db\fR and \fB\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db\fR select the IC database remotes\[char46] Their defaults are the corresponding local unix database sockets\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-ovn\-northd\-nb\-db=\fIPROTO\fB:\fIIP ADDRESS\fB:
\fIPORT\fB\[char46]\[char46]
\fR
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-ovn\-northd\-sb\-db=\fIPROTO\fB:\fIIP ADDRESS\fB:
\fIPORT\fB\[char46]\[char46]
\fR
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-ovn\-ic\-nb\-db=\fIPROTO\fB:\fIIP ADDRESS\fB:
\fIPORT\fB\[char46]\[char46]
\fR
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-ovn\-ic\-sb\-db=\fIPROTO\fB:\fIIP ADDRESS\fB:
\fIPORT\fB\[char46]\[char46]
\fR
.SH "CLUSTERING OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-nb\-election\-timer=\fITimeout in milliseconds\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-election\-timer=\fITimeout in milliseconds\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-local\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-local\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-local\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-local\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=\fIIP ADDRESS\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-port=\fIPORT NUMBER\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-ic\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-proto=\fIPROTO (tcp/ssl)\fB\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade=\fIyes|no\fB\fR controls whether clustered database servers automatically upgrade their schemas when they start\[char46] The default is \fByes\fR; specify \fBno\fR to disable the automatic upgrade\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade\fR is equivalent to \fB\-\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade=no\fR\[char46] The default is \fByes\fR\[char46]
.SH "PROBE INTERVAL OPTIONS"
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-db\-nb\-probe\-interval\-to\-active=\fITime in milliseconds\fB
\fR\[char46]
.PP
.PP
\fB
\-\-db\-sb\-probe\-interval\-to\-active=\fITime in milliseconds\fB
\fR\[char46]
.SH "RELAY OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR, \fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-pidfile=\fIFILE\fB\fR, and \fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-ctrl\-sock=\fISOCKET\fB\fR set the relay socket, pidfile, and control socket\[char46] The defaults are \fBovnsb_relay_db\[char46]sock\fR, \fBovnsb_relay_db\[char46]pid\fR, and \fBovnsb_relay_db\[char46]ctl\fR in \fBOVN_RUNDIR\fR\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-remote=\fIREMOTE\fB\fR selects the upstream relay remote\[char46] The default is empty\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-db\-sb\-relay\-use\-remote\-in\-db=\fIyes|no\fB\fR controls whether ovsdb-server listens on the Southbound remotes configured in the database \fBconnections\fR column\[char46] The default is \fByes\fR\[char46] A bare option is equivalent to specifying \fByes\fR\[char46]
.SH "EXTRA OPTIONS"
.PP
.PP
Any options after \(cq\-\(cq will be passed on to the binary run by \fIcommand\fR with the exception of start_northd, which can have options specified in ovn-northd-db-params\[char46]conf\[char46] Any \fIextra_args\fR passed to start_northd will be passed to the ovsdb-servers if \fB\-\-ovn\-manage\-ovsdb=yes\fR
.SH "CONFIGURATION FILES"
.PP
.PP
Following are the optional configuration files\[char46] If present, it should be located in the etc dir
.SS "ovnnb\-active\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, this file should hold the url to connect to the active Northbound DB server
.PP
\fBtcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6641\fR
.SS "ovnsb\-active\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, this file should hold the url to connect to the active Southbound DB server
.PP
\fBtcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6642\fR
.SS "ovn\-northd\-db\-params\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, start_northd will not start the DB server even if \fB\-\-ovn\-manage\-ovsdb=yes\fR\[char46] This file should hold the database url parameters to be passed to ovn-northd\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ovnnb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6641 \-\-ovnsb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6642\fR
.SS "ic\-nb\-active\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, this file should hold the url to connect to the active Interconnection Northbound DB server
.PP
\fBtcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6645\fR
.SS "ic\-sb\-active\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, this file should hold the url to connect to the active Interconnection Southbound DB server
.PP
\fBtcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6646\fR
.SS "ovn\-ic\-db\-params\[char46]conf"
.PP
.PP
If present, this file should hold the database url parameters to be passed to ovn-ic\[char46]
.PP
\fB\-\-ic\-nb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6645 \-\-ic\-sb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6646\fR
.SH "RUNNING OVN DB SERVERS WITHOUT DETACHING"
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl run_nb_ovsdb\fR
.PP
.PP
This command runs the OVN nb ovsdb-server without passing the \fBdetach\fR option, making it to block until ovsdb-server exits\[char46] This command will be useful for starting the OVN nb ovsdb-server in a container\[char46]
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl run_sb_ovsdb\fR
.PP
.PP
This command runs the OVN sb ovsdb-server without passing the \fBdetach\fR option, making it to block until ovsdb-server exits\[char46] This command will be useful for starting the OVN sb ovsdb-server in a container\[char46]
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl run_ic_nb_ovsdb\fR
.PP
.PP
This command runs the OVN IC-NB ovsdb-server without passing the \fBdetach\fR option, making it to block until ovsdb-server exits\[char46] This command will be useful for starting the OVN IC-NB ovsdb-server in a container\[char46]
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl run_ic_sb_ovsdb\fR
.PP
.PP
This command runs the OVN IC-SB ovsdb-server without passing the \fBdetach\fR option, making it to block until ovsdb-server exits\[char46] This command will be useful for starting the OVN IC-SB ovsdb-server in a container\[char46]
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl run_ovnbr_ovsdb\fR
.PP
.PP
This command runs the OVN bridge db ovsdb-server without passing the \fBdetach\fR option, making it to block until ovsdb-server exits\[char46] This command will be useful for starting the OVN br db ovsdb-server in a container\[char46]
.SH "EXAMPLE USAGE"
.SS "Run ovn\-controller on a host already running OVS"
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_controller\fR
.SS "Run ovn\-northd on a host already running OVS"
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_northd\fR
.SS "All\-in\-one OVS+OVN for testing"
.PP
\fB# ovs\-ctl start \-\-system\-id=\(dqrandom\(dq\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_northd\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_controller\fR
.SS "Promote and demote ovsdb servers"
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl promote_ovnnb\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl promote_ovnsb\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl \-\-db\-nb\-sync\-from\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-db\-nb\-sync\-from\-port=6641 \-\-db\-nb\-probe\-interval\-to\-active=60000 demote_ovnnb\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl \-\-db\-sb\-sync\-from\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-db\-sb\-sync\-from\-port=6642 \-\-db\-sb\-probe\-interval\-to\-active=60000 demote_ovnsb\fR
.SS "Creating a clustered db on 3 nodes with IPs x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x, y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y and z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z"
.ST "Starting OVN ovsdb servers and ovn-northd on the node with IP x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovn\-ctl \-\-db\-nb\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-db\-nb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-sb\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-db\-sb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-ovn\-northd\-nb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6641,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6641,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6641
\-\-ovn\-northd\-sb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6642,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6642,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6642
start_northd
\fR
.ST "Starting OVN ovsdb-servers and ovn-northd on the node with IP y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y and joining the cluster started at x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovn\-ctl \-\-db\-nb\-addr=y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y \-\-db\-nb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-sb\-addr=y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y \-\-db\-sb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y
\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y
\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-ovn\-northd\-nb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6641,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6641,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6641
\-\-ovn\-northd\-sb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6642,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6642,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6642
start_northd
\fR
.ST "Starting OVN ovsdb-servers and ovn-northd on the node with IP z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z and joining the cluster started at x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovn\-ctl \-\-db\-nb\-addr=z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z
\-\-db\-nb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z
\-\-db\-sb\-addr=z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z
\-\-db\-sb\-create\-insecure\-remote=yes
\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z
\-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-remote\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x
\-\-ovn\-northd\-nb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6641,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6641,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6641
\-\-ovn\-northd\-sb\-db=tcp:x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x:6642,tcp:y\[char46]y\[char46]y\[char46]y:6642,tcp:z\[char46]z\[char46]z\[char46]z:6642
start_northd
\fR
.SS "Passing ssl keys when starting OVN dbs will supersede the default ssl values in db"
.ST "Starting standalone ovn db server passing SSL/TLS certificates"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovn\-ctl \-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-key=/etc/ovn/ovnnb\-privkey\[char46]pem
\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-cert=/etc/ovn/ovnnb\-cert\[char46]pem
\-\-ovn\-nb\-db\-ssl\-ca\-cert=/etc/ovn/cacert\[char46]pem
\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-key=/etc/ovn/ovnsb\-privkey\[char46]pem
\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-cert=/etc/ovn/ovnsb\-cert\[char46]pem
\-\-ovn\-sb\-db\-ssl\-ca\-cert=/etc/ovn/cacert\[char46]pem
start_northd
\fR
.SS "Avoiding automatic clustered OVN database schema upgrade"
.PP
.PP
If you desire more control over clustered DB schema upgrade, you can opt-out of automatic on-start upgrade attempts with \fB\-\-no\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade\fR\[char46]
.ST "Start OVN NB and SB clustered databases on host with IP x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x without schema upgrade"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovn\-ctl start_nb_ovsdb \-\-db\-nb\-cluster\-local\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-no\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade
# ovn\-ctl start_sb_ovsdb \-\-db\-sb\-cluster\-local\-addr=x\[char46]x\[char46]x\[char46]x \-\-no\-db\-cluster\-schema\-upgrade
\fR
.ST "Trigger clustered DB schema upgrade manually"
.PP
.PP
\fB
# ovsdb\-client convert unix:/var/run/ovn/ovnnb_db\[char46]sock /usr/local/share/ovn/ovn\-nb\[char46]ovsschema
# ovsdb\-client convert unix:/var/run/ovn/ovnsb_db\[char46]sock /usr/local/share/ovn/ovn\-sb\[char46]ovsschema
\fR
.SS "Run OVN bridge controller services on a host already running OVS"
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_ovnbr_ovsdb\fR
.PP
\fB# ovn\-ctl start_br_controller\fR
